/* 段落记忆 · 词层 3 · 子块 c：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(3,{"sub":"c","par":{"multiple":{"tw":[["single",1],["multiply",4],["double",5],["triple",5],["multiplicity",4],["various",6],["numerous",6]],"en":"The teacher wrote a single number on the board and asked how it would multiply. The answer was not one value but multiple ones. If we double the first number we get one result, and if we triple it we get another. A multiplicity of answers, she said, is normal in real problems. The class then looked at various examples taken from a market: numerous small prices, each with its own rule. My partner counted on paper while I used the calculator. In the end we found three correct answers, and the teacher said that was exactly the point of the lesson.","zh":"老师在黑板上写了一个数，问它乘起来会怎样。答案不是一个值，而是好几个。把第一个数翻倍得到一种结果，乘以三又得到另一种。她说，答案多得很，这在真问题里很正常。接着全班看了从市场里取来的各种例子：数目众多的小价格，每个都按自己的规矩走。我的搭档用纸算，我用计算器。最后我们找出三个正确答案，老师说，这节课要讲的正是这一点。"},"neglect":{"tw":[["negligent",4],["drop",0],["jump",3],["miss",3],["forget",3],["fail",0],["decline",2],["abuse",6]],"en":"For years the town neglected its old bridge. A negligent repair in the 1990s left a crack that nobody wrote down. Drivers would drop coins into the gap for luck, and children would jump on the loose stones. When one school bus had to miss its usual road for a week, people finally began to talk. The council could not forget the letters from parents, and could not fail to act twice. The decline of the bridge became the first point of every meeting. Experts warned against the abuse of the small budget, and work started in March.","zh":"多年来镇上一直没管那座老桥。九十年代一次马虎的修补留下了一道缝，谁也没记下来。司机往缝里丢硬币讨吉利，孩子们在松动的石头上跳。等一辆校车不得不改道一周之后，人们才终于议论起来。市政会没法忘掉家长们的来信，也不可能再拖着不动。这座桥的衰败成了每次会上的第一个议题。专家提醒不要滥用那点有限的预算，工程三月开工了。"},"permit":{"tw":[["permissible",4],["allow",3],["admit",3],["accept",2],["forbid",1],["apply",6],["permissive",4],["licence",0],["pass",3],["obtain",6],["permission",4]],"en":"A young driver went to the office to obtain a permit for his small truck. The clerk asked him to apply in person and to show a licence with his photo. 'It is permissible,' she said, 'to park here, but you may not pass the bridge with a heavy load.' He had to accept the rule, even though it seemed strict. His father, who was more permissive, told him to just argue and ask for permission again. The office would not allow that; they would not admit any visitor without a pass. One thing was certain: the law could forbid a truck on that narrow road. In the end he left with the paper in his hand.","zh":"一个年轻司机去办事处，想给自己的小货车办一张许可证。办事员让他本人来申请，还要出示带照片的执照。她说，'停在这儿是允许的，但载重货不许过桥。'他只好接受这条规定，尽管它看着挺严。他父亲比较宽容，让他干脆去争一争，再求一次许可。办事处不肯松口；没有通行证，谁也不让进。有一点是肯定的：法律可以禁止货车走那条窄路。最后他攥着那张纸走了出来。"},"pursue":{"tw":[["pursuit",4],["follow",0],["close",3],["act",2],["establish",6],["pursuant",4],["engage",0],["chase",3],["travel",2],["seek",6],["prosecute",0]],"en":"For two days the police would pursue a stolen car along the coast road. They had to follow it close, never letting the gap grow. The chase passed three small towns and a long bridge. Pursuant to the new law, officers could not engage a fleeing driver at high speed. So the officers chose to travel slowly and seek a safer moment. The pursuit ended at a farm gate, where the driver gave up. Later the court would prosecute him for theft. The inspector said they also wanted to establish how the car had been taken, and the case would act as a warning to others.","zh":"一连两天，警察沿着海岸公路追一辆失窃的车。他们得紧紧跟着，不让距离拉大。这场追逐穿过三个小镇和一座长桥。依照新法律，警员不得高速与逃跑的司机缠斗。于是他们选择慢慢开，寻找更稳妥的时机。追捕在一处农庄门口结束，司机在那里放弃了。后来法庭要以盗窃罪起诉他。探长说，他们还想查明这车是怎么被弄走的，而这个案子会给别人一个警告。"},"radiate":{"tw":[["radiance",4],["shine",0],["flash",3],["change",2],["diffuse",6],["radiator",4],["beam",0],["gleam",3],["feel",2],["condense",6],["glow",3]],"en":"On the coldest morning of the year, an old radiator began to radiate heat into the small kitchen. Outside, the sun started to shine over the frozen lake, and its radiance filled the whole valley. A single beam crossed the window and made a thin gleam on the floor. For a moment a bright flash of light came off the ice, so strong that I could feel it warm my face. The heat seemed to diffuse through the room and change the cold air. Later the steam from my cup began to condense on the glass. Slowly the kitchen took on a soft orange glow. It was a good way to start a winter day.","zh":"一年里最冷的那个早上，一台旧暖气片开始往小厨房里散热。外面，太阳从冰封的湖面上升起，它的光辉铺满了整个山谷。一道光柱穿过窗户，在地板上落下一丝微光。有一瞬，冰面上迸出一道亮闪闪的光，强得我都能感到它把脸烘暖了。热气似乎在屋里弥散开来，把冷空气也变了。后来，我杯子里冒出的蒸汽开始在玻璃上凝结。厨房慢慢泛起一层柔和的橘色光晕。这样开始一个冬日，挺好。"},"origin":{"tw":[["originate",4],["line",0],["cause",3],["ancestry",2],["surname",6],["genetic",4],["root",0],["home",3],["identity",6],["stock",0]],"en":"My grandmother spent years tracing the origin of our family name. She would start with a single line on a paper and follow it back through old records. The cause of her search was a letter found in the attic of her home. She learned that our surname had once been spelled quite differently. Old papers told her about our ancestry, and a modern test showed a genetic link to a village far away. The root of the whole story, she said, was one village where the name seemed to originate. That search gave her a new sense of identity, and it also gave the family a story to pass on. The old stock had travelled far, but it had not been lost.","zh":"我奶奶花了好些年，追溯我们家姓氏的起源。她总是从纸上的一行字开始，顺着旧档案一路往回查。她动这个念头的起因，是在自家阁楼里发现的一封信。她得知，我们的姓从前拼法完全不同。旧文书讲了我们祖先的事，而一次现代检测显示出与一个遥远村落的血缘关联。她说，整个故事的根，是一个似乎源自那里的名字。那次寻访让她对身份有了新的认识，也给家里留下了一个可以传下去的故事。这门老血脉走了很远，却没有丢掉。"},"perceive":{"tw":[["perception",4],["comprehend",0],["catch",3],["understand",2],["imply",6],["perceptible",4],["feel",3],["perceptive",4]],"en":"A good listener can perceive things that others simply miss. She may catch the quiet note under the drum, or feel the small pause before the chorus. Such a perceptive ear does not come at once; it grows with practice. Her perception of a piece is often deeper than mine. I could not comprehend how she heard all that, and her answer would imply hours of careful work. The change in the room was hardly perceptible, yet she noticed it at once. To understand music, she says, you must first learn to be still. I try to remember that whenever a song begins.","zh":"好的听者能觉察到别人干脆漏掉的东西。她能在鼓声底下抓住那个轻音符，或是感到副歌前那一小段停顿。这样一副敏锐的耳朵不是一下子就有了，是靠练出来的。她对一支曲子的知觉，常常比我深。我没法领会她怎么能听出这些，而她的回答往往意味着好几个钟头的用心。屋里那点变化几乎察觉不到，她却立刻注意到了。她说，要听懂音乐，得先学会静下来。每次一首歌响起，我都尽量记着这句话。"},"perception":{"tw":[["perceive",4],["smell",3],["cognition",2],["sense",6],["perceptual",4],["taste",3],["inherent",6],["perceptive",4]],"en":"A chef's perception grows sharper with every year in the kitchen. He can perceive a change in a sauce before anyone else, and his sense of smell is his best tool. Taste, he says, is a kind of cognition that no book can teach. His perceptual skills come from long hours at the same stove. Some of it seems inherent, but most is simple practice. When a dish is wrong, he can tell at once, and a perceptive guest will notice too. He would rather trust his nose than a clock. 'Cook with your eyes closed,' he tells us, 'and you will learn to feel the food.'","zh":"厨师的感觉，在厨房里一年比一年敏锐。一锅酱汁有了变化，他总能比别人先察觉，而嗅觉是他最好的工具。他说，味觉是一种书本教不了的认知。他那套知觉的本领，来自长年在同一口灶边的打磨。其中有些像是天生的，但多半只是练出来的。一道菜不对，他立刻就能尝出来，一位敏锐的客人也会注意到。他宁可相信鼻子，也不信钟表。他说，'闭上眼睛做菜，你就会学会用感觉去摸食物。'"},"proceed":{"tw":[["procedure",4],["continue",0],["work",3],["happen",2],["intend",6],["procession",4],["move",0],["travel",2],["initiate",6]],"en":"Every spring a long procession moves slowly through the old town. The rule is simple: the leaders must proceed first, and the rest will follow in pairs. No one intends to hurry, because the whole point is to be seen. As they travel down the main street, shopkeepers continue their work at the doors. If a small thing should happen, the marshals know the procedure and step in at once. They will initiate the song only when the last cart can move again. Later, the townspeople gather in the square and wait for the food. It is the same ritual year after year, and no one wants it to end.","zh":"每年春天，一支长长的游行队伍都会慢慢穿过老城。规矩很简单：领头的人先走，其余的人成对跟上。谁也不想赶，因为这件事的意义就在于被人看见。他们沿着主街往前走时，店主们照旧在门口干活。万一出点小事，负责维持的人清楚该走的程序，立刻就会上前。直到最后一辆大车又能挪动，他们才会起头唱歌。之后，镇民们聚到广场上，等着开饭。年年都是同样的仪式，谁也不想让它结束。"},"mode":{"tw":[["modal",4],["fashion",0],["fit",3],["condition",2],["interface",6],["manner",0],["form",3],["property",2],["dynamic",6],["style",0]],"en":"The new app has a simple mode for older users. In this form, the interface shows only three buttons and no small text. The style is plain, and every word appears in the same manner on each page. You can switch to a dynamic mode that fits the screen to any size. The engineers say the property of a good design is that it works in any condition, even with a weak signal. A modal box appears only when you must choose between two actions. My aunt likes the fashion of the old paper form, so she prints hers at the shop. The app, she admits, is a better fit for her hands.","zh":"这款新应用给年长的用户留了一个简单的模式。在这个形式里，界面只显示三个按钮，没有小字。风格朴素，每页上每个词都以同样的样式出现。你可以切到一个动态模式，让界面适应任何尺寸。工程师们说，好设计的一个特性就是：不论在什么条件下都能用，哪怕信号很弱。只有当你必须在两个操作之间二选一时，才会弹出模态框。我姑妈喜欢旧纸质表格的那种样子，所以她的表在店里打印。她承认，这应用对她这双手来说更合适。"},"moderate":{"tw":[["moderation",4],["chair",0],["catch",3],["change",2],["strong",6],["check",0],["train",3],["adult",2],["contrast",6],["control",0]],"en":"At the community centre a doctor would chair a meeting about healthy habits. Her advice was simple: keep exercise moderate, and eat with moderation. She told us that an adult who trains too hard can catch a cold more easily. A strong body is not built in a week, and the contrast between rest and work matters. We should check our pulse and change our plan when we feel tired. In moderation lies control, she said, not weakness. After the talk, a few of us stayed to ask how to begin. She smiled and said: start with a short walk after dinner.","zh":"在社区中心，一位医生主持了一场关于健康习惯的座谈。她的建议很简单：运动要适度，吃东西要有节制。她告诉我们，一个练得过猛的成年人，反而更容易感冒。强健的身体不是一个星期练出来的，休息和工作之间的对照很重要。我们该查一查自己的脉搏，感到累时就调整计划。她说，节制里藏着的是掌控，而不是软弱。讲座结束后，我们几个人留下来问该怎么开始。她笑着说：晚饭后先走一小段。"},"negative":{"tw":[["negate",4],["minus",5],["kill",3],["film",2],["positive",1],["impact",6],["veto",0],["nay",3],["oppose",2],["factor",6]],"en":"The old photographer kept a box of negatives in his drawer. Each film held one memory, and a negative could show a face better than any new print. In his shop the answer to a hard question was often a quiet nay. He would never negate a young person's idea without a reason, yet he could oppose a bad plan with one look. When the town council met, he would veto nothing himself; he only watched. A minus sign on the account was not always a bad thing, he said; it could kill a wrong plan before it grew. The impact of one vote was another factor to consider. His own pictures had more positive energy than he admitted.","zh":"那位老摄影师在抽屉里留着一盒底片。每卷胶片都藏着一段记忆，而一张底片有时比任何新洗出来的照片都更能显出人的面容。在他店里，难题的答案常常是一声轻轻的'不'。他不会无缘无故地否定年轻人的想法，可一个眼神就能反对一个坏主意。镇议会开会时，他自己什么都不会否决，只是看着。他说，账上出现一个负号并不总是坏事。一票的影响也是另一个要考虑的因素。他那些照片里的正能量，比他嘴上承认的要多。"},"institute":{"tw":[["institution",4],["bring",0],["fix",3],["initiate",2],["research",6],["plant",0],["appoint",3],["science",6],["establish",0]],"en":"Twenty years ago a group of teachers decided to establish a small institute for the study of soil. They had little money and no building, so they began to bring old tools from home. Their first research was simple: how does salt move through wet ground? Later the group would initiate a long study of local plants and fix a small lab in the corner of a hall. A young scientist was appointed to run the tests. Over time the institute grew into a real institution, known for honest work. It never lost the habit of asking plain questions. That, its founder said, is the heart of good science.","zh":"二十年前，一群教师决定创办一个小研究所，专门研究土壤。他们钱很少，也没有房子，于是开始从家里搬来旧工具。他们头一项研究很简单：盐在湿土里是怎么移动的？后来这群人又发起了一项对本地植物的长期研究，还在走廊一角收拾出一间小实验室。一位年轻科学家被派来负责那些测试。时间一长，研究所长成了一家真正的机构，以老实做学问出名。它始终没丢掉问平常问题的习惯。它的创办人说，这正是好科学的根本。"},"integrate":{"tw":[["integral",4],["mix",0],["fold",3],["compound",2],["differentiate",1],["enable",6],["incorporate",0],["unify",3],["transform",6]],"en":"When two small schools joined, the teachers had to integrate their classes. The head wanted one integral plan, not two separate ones, so the work began with a long meeting. A simple rule would enable the children to mix without fear, and each class would incorporate the best ideas of both. Teachers learned to fold new topics into old lessons and to treat each room as part of one compound. Hard as it was, they would not differentiate between the two groups in any test. Slowly the separate habits began to unify. By the second year you could not tell which child came from which school. The change would transform the whole village.","zh":"两所小学校合并后，老师们得把各自的班级整合到一起。校长想要一套完整的方案，而不是两套分开的，所以事情从一场长会开始。一条简单的规矩就能让孩子们放心地混在一起。老师们学会把新内容折进旧课里，把每间教室都当作同一个大院子的一部分。尽管很难，他们在任何测验里都不区分这两个群体。渐渐地，两套分开的习惯合到了一起。到第二年，谁也看不出哪个孩子来自哪所学校。这场变化会改变整个村子。"},"occupy":{"tw":[["occupation",4],["busy",0],["involve",3],["use",2],["reside",6],["concern",0],["crash",3],["work",2],["interest",2]],"en":"When we moved into the old farmhouse, boxes seemed to occupy every corner. The whole family was busy for a week, and each room would involve a small fight about where things should go. We had to use the barn for the things we could not fit inside, and my grandparents would reside in the quiet back room. One of my concerns was the hot water, which never worked before noon. Then a box fell with a crash, and we all laughed. For my sister, whose occupation is teaching, the long holiday was welcome. Her main interest was the garden by the gate.","zh":"我们搬进那座老农舍时，箱子似乎占满了每个角落。全家忙了一个星期，每间屋子都会为东西该放哪儿闹点小争执。放不进屋里的东西只好搁进谷仓，我的祖父母则住进安静的后间。我操心的一件事是热水，中午之前从不热。后来一只箱子哗啦一声倒下，我们都笑了。我姐姐的职业是教书，这个长假对她正好。她最感兴趣的是大门口那片园子。"},"persuade":{"tw":[["persuasion",4],["carry",0],["sell",3],["influence",2],["dissuade",1],["convince",6],["sway",0],["assure",3],["urge",6]],"en":"My uncle wanted to sell the small house near the river. A young agent tried to persuade him to ask a higher price. She had a smooth way of talking, and her persuasion was not always honest. She would carry a folder of old photos and use them to influence the buyer. Yet my uncle would not let her sway him, and no one could dissuade him from his own plan. He asked her to convince him with real numbers, not with smiles. He also had to assure the buyer that the roof was sound. In the end he would urge her to take a lower price, because he wanted a quick sale.","zh":"我叔叔想把河边那栋小房子卖掉。一个年轻中介劝他把价钱要得高些。她嘴皮子很滑，那套劝说的功夫并不总是老实。她会揣着一叠旧照片，用它们去影响买主。可我叔叔不肯让她说动，谁也没法让他放弃自己的打算。他让她用真凭实据来说服他，而不是靠笑脸。他还得让买主放心，屋顶是结实的。最后他反过来劝她接受一个更低的价钱，因为他想快点成交。"},"precede":{"tw":[["predecessor",4],["lead",3],["lie",2],["follow",1],["convene",6],["premise",0],["state",2],["converge",6],["preface",0]],"en":"At the school ceremony a short speech would precede the dinner. My predecessor in the job had planned the whole evening, and I had to follow her careful notes. The guests would convene in the hall at six, and the meal would lead into a round of songs. In the preface of the program, a line stated the date and the name of the old head teacher. The premise behind the plan was simple: everyone should feel welcome. As the evening went on, all the small talks seemed to converge into one warm noise. In the corner a few old photos lay on a table. I hoped the evening would not disappoint the school.","zh":"学校的典礼上，会先有一段简短的致辞，然后才开饭。我这个岗位的前任早把整晚都安排好了，我只好照着她细致的笔记来。客人们六点到礼堂集合，饭后转入一轮唱歌。节目单的前言里，写明了日期和老校长的名字。这套安排背后的前提很简单：每个人都该觉得受欢迎。随着夜色渐深，那些细碎的交谈仿佛汇成了一片暖暖的喧响。角落里的一张桌上，摊着几张旧照片。"},"procedure":{"tw":[["proceed",4],["process",0],["rule",3],["software",2],["diagnosis",6],["function",0],["condition",3],["surgery",6],["routine",3]],"en":"At the hospital a strict procedure controls every step of the day. First the nurse checks the software that reads each patient's condition. Then the doctor makes a diagnosis and decides how the process should proceed. Before any surgery, the team follows an old rule: count the tools twice. The whole thing has become a routine, yet no one takes it lightly. Each part of the machine has a function, and a single fault can slow everything down. After the operation the patient must rest for a week. The nurses say the calm of a good team is the best medicine of all.","zh":"在医院里，一套严格的程序管着一天的每一步。护士先检查读病人各项状况的软件。接着医生作出诊断，决定整个流程该怎么往下走。任何一次手术之前，团队都守着一条老规矩：工具数两遍。整套做法已经成了常规，可谁也不敢马虎。机器上每个零件都有它的功用，一处小毛病就能让一切都慢下来。手术后，病人得休息一个星期。护士们说，一个团队沉稳有序，才是最好的药。"},"provision":{"tw":[["provide",4],["supply",2],["issue",3],["store",2],["repeal",6],["proviso",0],["condition",2],["tax",6],["purvey",0]],"en":"The town made a provision of grain and oil for the poorest families each winter. A local farmer would provide fresh vegetables, and a shop would supply the rest. Workers had to issue a card to every household, and a small store held the goods until spring. There was one proviso in the rule: only those who lived in the town could apply. Some people wanted to repeal the old tax that paid for the whole plan. The condition was simple enough, but the money was always short. A young couple helped to purvey the food to the far streets. By March the shelves were empty again.","zh":"每年冬天，镇上为最穷的人家备下一批粮食和油。本地一个农夫提供新鲜蔬菜，一家店铺供应其余的。工作人员得给每户发一张卡，一个小仓房把东西存到开春。规矩里有这么一条附加条件：只有住在镇上的人才能申请。有人想废除那项为整件事出钱的旧税。条件本身不难，可钱总是紧。一对年轻夫妇帮着把食物送到偏远的街巷。到三月，货架又空了。"},"publish":{"tw":[["publication",4],["issue",0],["gazette",3],["produce",2],["copy",6],["write",0],["publicize",2],["document",6],["print",0]],"en":"For thirty years the same family would publish a small weekly paper. The first publication came out on a single sheet, and the editor had to write every line himself. Later they would print more pages and produce a full issue each Friday. A local gazette, as they called it, was read in every shop on the street. To publicize a lost dog, people would send a note to the office. The old editor kept a document for each year and a copy of every photograph. He said a good paper must serve the town, not the owner. The last print run came when the machines finally wore out.","zh":"三十年来，同一家人一直出版一份小周报。头一期只印在一张纸上，编辑每一行都得自己写。后来他们加了几页，每周五出一期完整的。他们管它叫本地公报，街上每家店都看。要找一条走失的狗，人们就写张条子送到编辑部。老编辑每年留一份文件，每张照片都留一份底子。他说，好报纸该为镇子做事，而不是替老板做事。最后一版印出来时，机器终于磨坏了。"},"joint":{"tw":[["join",0],["elbow",3],["cut",2],["separate",1],["alliance",6],["stick",0],["hinge",3],["fit",2],["major",6],["articulate",0]],"en":"The old carpenter would join two pieces of wood at a single joint. He liked to cut each end himself and to check that they would fit without a gap. A small hinge, rather than a nail, was his way to let one part move. He would stick the parts with a warm glue and hold them still until it dried. For a major table he would rest his elbow on the bench and count each part of the design before he began. Wood and glue form a quiet alliance, he said, and a good joint will not separate with the years. Then he would articulate the whole plan for his young helper. Measure twice, he told him, and cut once.","zh":"老木匠会把两块木料接在一个接头上。他喜欢自己刨两端的口子，再检查能不能严丝合缝。他会用一只小铰链而不是钉子，让其中一部分能活动。他用温热的胶把部件粘住，按着不动直到干透。做大桌子时，他会把胳膊肘撑在长凳上，先数清设计里的每一部分。他说，木料和胶合成一种安静的同盟，好的接头经年也不会分开。然后他又把整份打算一五一十地讲给年轻帮手听。他叮嘱他，量两遍，切一次。"},"lodge":{"tw":[["charge",0],["hunt",3],["house",2],["dislodge",1],["inn",6],["club",0],["quarter",3],["accuse",2],["hill",6],["order",0]],"en":"The old lodge stood alone on a bare hill above the valley. It had once been a hunting house for a rich family, and now it worked as a small inn for travellers. A club of walkers used the west quarter as their home base each summer. The owner would charge a fair price for a bed, and he kept good order in the dining room. One night a guest tried to accuse a young cook of theft. The owner would not let anger dislodge his calm. He called a hunt through the kitchen and found the missing watch under a chair. Nothing more was said, and the guest left quietly.","zh":"那座老旅舍孤零零地立在山谷上方一座光秃秃的小山岗上。它从前是富人家的猎屋，如今成了一家接待过路人的小客栈。每年夏天，一个徒步者俱乐部把西边那几间当作大本营。老板收公道的住店钱，饭厅里也维持着好秩序。一天夜里，一位客人想诬告一名年轻厨子偷东西。老板不肯让怒气搅乱自己的镇定。他把厨房翻了一遍，在椅子底下找到了那块丢失的表。谁也没再多说什么，客人悄悄走了。"},"net":{"tw":[["clear",5],["cage",3],["catch",2],["gross",1],["profit",6],["final",0],["dividend",3],["goal",2],["quarter",6],["last",0]],"en":"The fishing co-op rose before dawn and mended its long net by the light of one lamp. The catch that morning was small, but the cage of crabs made up for it. At the end of the quarter the old clerk wrote the gross takings on a clear page, then took away the cost of fuel. What was left was the net profit, and it was the final figure that mattered. Their goal was simple: a fair dividend for every boat. The last line of the page showed that the money was real.","zh":"天没亮，渔业合作社就起来了，就着一盏灯修补那张长网。那天早上捕的鱼不多，可一笼螃蟹补上了。季度末，老账房把毛收入写在一张清清爽爽的纸上，再扣掉油钱。剩下的就是净利，而这最后这个数字才是要紧的。他们的目标很简单：给每条船一份公道的分红。纸上最后一行说明，这笔钱是真的。"},"profit":{"tw":[["benefit",0],["account",3],["advantage",2],["lose",1],["share",6],["gain",2],["pyramid",3],["income",2],["quarter",6],["net",3]],"en":"My cousin opened a small bakery and hoped to make a profit in her first quarter. She kept every account by hand and gave each worker a share. There was some benefit in buying flour in bulk, an advantage she had learned from her mother. But one winter she began to lose money, and a friend tried to push her into a pyramid scheme. She refused, even though the offer sounded easy. Her income slowly returned, and she netted a small gain by spring. In the end the profit was modest, yet it was hers.","zh":"我表姐开了家小面包铺，指望头一个季度就能盈利。她每一笔账都记在本子上，还分给每个工人一份。整袋买面粉有点好处，这是她从母亲那儿学来的一手。可有一年冬天她开始赔钱，一个朋友还想拉她去搞什么金字塔式的传销。她没答应，虽然那提议听着挺轻松。她的进项慢慢回来了，到春天居然还小赚了一笔。到头来利润不算多，可那是她自己的。"},"layer":{"tw":[["lay",4],["bed",0],["course",3],["shape",2],["thick",6],["lift",3],["region",2],["fluid",6]],"en":"On the cliff face you can see one layer of rock above another. Below lies a thick bed of red stone, laid down when this whole region was under the sea. A softer course of grey rock sits on top, and its shape tells a long story. A young student would lift a piece and test it with water to see how it held the fluid. The bottom layer was the oldest, the top the newest. Wind and rain had worn each one in a different way. She wrote in her notes that time here is measured in layers. Then she climbed back up the long path.","zh":"在崖壁上，你能看到一层岩石叠在另一层上面。底下是一层厚厚的红石，是这个地区还沉在海里时沉积下来的。上面压着一层软一些的灰岩，它的形状讲着一段很长的故事。一个年轻学生会拿起一块，用水试一试它怎么留住液体。最底下那层最古老，最上面那层最新。风与雨把每一层都磨成了不同的样子。她在笔记里写道，这里的时间是按层来计的。然后她顺着那条长路爬了回去。"},"liberate":{"tw":[["liberty",4],["free",2],["run",3],["subjugate",6],["loose",0],["parole",3],["enslave",6],["release",0]],"en":"One spring the workers at the old camp decided to liberate a group of birds kept in small cages. It was not about their own liberty; it was about giving the birds a free sky. A thin rope was still loose on the gate, and one bird would run along the top and refuse to go. For years people had tried to subjugate these animals and treat them as tools. Then a young keeper got an early parole from his own duty and came to help. He opened each cage and let the birds release their fear into the air. Nobody tried to enslave them again. That evening the whole yard was quiet and full of wings.","zh":"有一年春天，这个旧营地的工作人员决定把一群关在小笼子里的鸟放掉。这跟他们自己的自由无关；是要给这些鸟一片自由的天空。门上还松着一根细绳，有只鸟总沿着笼顶跑来跑去，不肯走。多年来，人们一直想驯服这些动物，把它们当工具使。后来一个年轻看守提早结束了自己的差事，赶来帮忙。他一个个打开笼门，让鸟把害怕撒进空中。再没人想去奴役它们了。那天傍晚，整个院子安静极了，满是翅膀。"},"passage":{"tw":[["pass",4],["transit",0],["throat",3],["journey",2],["swift",6],["channel",3],["section",2],["compromise",6]],"en":"The narrow passage between the two cliffs leads from the sea into a quiet bay. A swift tide runs through it, and ships must pass at the right hour. On the last journey of the season our captain waited a whole day for the water to turn. The channel is so tight that the boat seemed to move through the throat of a stone giant. A young sailor read one section of the old map aloud and noted the hours of safe transit. The captain was careful and would make no compromise with the sea. In the calm bay we rested for a night. At dawn we went on, and the passage lay behind us.","zh":"两片崖壁之间那条窄窄的通道，从海上通向一处宁静的海湾。湍急的潮水从中穿过，船必须在对的时辰才过。这个季节最后一趟航程里，船长等了整整一天，等水转向。航道太窄，船仿佛是从一个石头巨人的喉咙里穿过。一个年轻水手大声念出旧海图上的一个段落，还记下安全通行的那几个钟头。船长很谨慎，绝不肯对大海让半分步。在那片平静的海湾里，我们歇了一夜。天亮时我们继续走，通道已经落在身后。"},"poll":{"tw":[["pollster",4],["crown",0],["count",2],["survey",6],["canvass",0],["top",2],["tally",6],["pate",0]],"en":"On voting day the pollster stood at the gate with a long list. She would canvass every street before noon, asking each neighbour to join the survey. At the top of her page she kept a tally of the names she had. An old man scratched his pate and asked whether his vote would count. He tipped the crown of his hat and said the whole town talked of nothing else. By evening the poll had closed, and the final count was close. Nobody could say for certain who had won. The pollster folded her paper and went home.","zh":"投票那天，民调员在大门口站着，手里拿着一张长名单。她要在中午前跑遍每条街，请每一位邻居参加这次调查。她在纸的最上头记着已有名字的数目。一位老人挠了挠脑袋，问自己这一票算不算数。他把帽顶往上推了推，说全镇上下都在谈这件事。到傍晚，投票结束，最后的计票非常接近。谁也说不准究竟谁赢了。民调员合上纸，回了家。"},"initiate":{"tw":[["start",0],["cover",3],["admit",2],["expedite",6],["originate",0],["stage",3],["cause",2],["proceed",6],["pioneer",0]],"en":"The town will initiate a clean-up along the river next spring. We start with the worst part, where old waste covers the stones. The council had to admit that the work would take months. A small group will expedite the first days and stage a public meeting. The plan will originate in the schools, where children learn to care. The cause is simple: a river should not carry plastic to the sea. One pioneer of the idea was a quiet teacher. The first bags were heavy with wet bottles. Once we proceed, others will follow and help.","zh":"镇里明年春天要在河边发起一次清理。我们从最糟的一段开始，那里旧垃圾盖住了石头。议会不得不承认，这活得干上好几个月。一小拨人会加快头几天的进度，还办一场公开的说明会。这计划将从学校发端，让孩子们从小学会爱护。缘由很简单：一条河不该把塑料带进海里。最早想出这主意的是位安静的老师。我们一动手，别人就会跟上来帮忙。"},"input":{"tw":[["comment",0],["kick",3],["signal",2],["function",6],["remark",0],["mention",3],["component",2],["external",6],["stimulant",0]],"en":"Before the vote the editors asked for public input on the new plan. Readers could leave a comment or a short remark under each page. One small component of the system would turn every signal into a clear chart. The manager did not mention the cost, which was a mistake. We had to check each external plug before it could function. A warm cup of tea acted as a mild stimulant during the long night. One reader gave the whole idea a real kick with a single line. Their input changed the final design.","zh":"投票之前，编辑就新方案征求公众的意见。读者可以在每页下面留一条评论或一句短话。系统里一个小小的部件会把每道信号变成清楚的图表。经理没提成本，这是个错。每个外接插头都得先检查，它才能正常工作。漫长的夜里，一杯热茶成了温和的兴奋剂。有位读者只用一句话，就给了整个想法一记猛推。他们的意见改变了最后的设计。"},"insert":{"tw":[["enter",0],["cup",3],["add",2],["delete",6],["introduce",0],["feed",3],["break",2],["template",6],["enclose",0]],"en":"Please insert the date at the top of the page before you print. First enter your name in the small box below. Then add a short title and a line of address. Do not delete any part of the template. The form looked simple, but every line had a rule. We have to introduce the new form to every office. A thin sheet will enclose the letter and protect it in the post. My colleague had to feed the machine slowly so the paper would not break. She took a cup of coffee while the printer worked.","zh":"打印之前，请在页面顶端插入日期。先在下面那个小框里输入你的名字。然后加一个短标题和一行地址。模板的任何部分都别删。我们得把这张新表格介绍给每个办公室。一张薄纸会把信包在里面，寄的时候护着它。我的同事只好慢慢送纸，免得纸卡断。打印机干活时，她喝了杯咖啡。"},"inspire":{"tw":[["cheer",0],["encourage",3],["breathe",2],["desire",6],["prompt",0],["puff",3],["occasion",2],["embrace",6],["urge",0]],"en":"A single old painting could inspire a whole class of young artists. Our teacher would encourage us to breathe slowly and look again. She had a strong desire to cheer every shy student. On one special occasion she would prompt us to copy a small part. Two girls began to embrace the work with real joy. We would puff out our cheeks and laugh at our first tries. Her quiet urge to try again stayed with me for years. In the end we all made one picture we were proud of.","zh":"一幅旧画就能让一整班年轻画者受到启发。老师会鼓励我们慢慢呼吸，再看一遍。她很想给每个害羞的学生打气。有一次特别的场合，她会提点我们照着画一小块。两个姑娘开始满心欢喜地拥抱这项工作。我们会鼓起腮帮子，笑自己头一回的笨拙。她那句再来一次的催促，跟了我好多年。最后我们都画出了一张自己满意的画。"},"interior":{"tw":[["home",0],["belly",3],["surface",2],["exterior",1],["minister",6],["inside",5],["midst",3],["ministry",6],["internal",5]],"en":"The interior of the old house needed a fresh coat of paint. Its exterior was fine, but inside the walls were cold and damp. The surface of every room had small marks near the floor. My aunt said the belly of the building needed care most. We wanted to make the old place feel like home again. We stood in the midst of boxes and made a simple plan. A neighbour who worked at the ministry of the small church came to help with the colours. She was, in truth, no minister, just a patient friend, and her internal calm made the whole job easy.","zh":"这座老房子的内部需要重新刷一层漆。外面还过得去，可里面又冷又潮。每个房间的墙面靠地板处都有些印子。婶婶说，这屋子的肚腹最需要照顾。我们想让这老地方重新像个家。我们站在一堆箱子当中，定了个简单的方案。一位在附近小教堂的教会里做事的邻居来帮我们挑颜色。其实她并不是什么牧师，只是个有耐心的朋友，她那份内里的沉静让整件活都轻松了。"},"interpret":{"tw":[["read",3],["draw",3],["explain",2],["dictate",6],["see",0],["paint",3],["perform",2],["relate",6],["understand",2]],"en":"In the old hall the students had to interpret a famous painting for the class. One girl could read the whole story from the colours alone. She would explain how the artist chose to paint light on the water. Her teacher had to dictate a few facts before each talk. It was hard to see the meaning at first, but she made us understand. Later a small group would perform a short play about the same scene. The two works relate in a simple way: both ask what we truly see. Even the shy boy could draw one line from it.","zh":"在那间老厅里，学生们得为全班解读一幅名画。一个女孩光凭颜色就能读出整个故事。她会解释画家为什么那样画水上的光。每次开讲前，老师都得口述几点事实。一开始很难看出其中的意思，她却让我们明白了。后来一小群人把同一个情景演成了短剧。两件作品之间有很简单的关联：它们都在问我们究竟看见了什么。就连那个害羞的男孩也能从里面画出一条线。"},"invest":{"tw":[["seat",0],["cover",3],["spend",2],["divest",1],["buy",6],["gift",0],["crown",3],["borrow",6],["endow",0]],"en":"The family decided to invest their savings in a small workshop. They would spend a little each month on tools and wood. A kind uncle would endow the first machine as a gift. They had to borrow the rest from the bank. My father said it was wise to buy the best saw and to cover it well. In time they bought a second seat for the old truck. The shop would crown their long years of hard work. Later they chose to divest one part of the business and keep the rest.","zh":"一家人决定把积蓄投进一间小作坊。他们每个月会花一点钱买工具和木料。一位好心的叔叔把第一台机器作为礼物赠给他们。其余的他们只好向银行借。父亲说，买最好的锯子、好好保养它才明智。后来他们又给那辆旧卡车添了一个座位。这间铺子给他们多年的辛苦戴上了桂冠。再后来，他们选择卖掉生意的一部分，留下其余。"},"justify":{"tw":[["excuse",3],["legitimate",3],["adjust",2],["intent",6],["free",0],["plead",3],["confirm",2],["pretext",6],["warrant",0]],"en":"The owner tried to justify the high price of the bread. He would plead that the flour had grown dear, but no warrant could confirm his claim. A fair judge asked him to adjust his numbers. The people wanted a legitimate reason, not a weak excuse. He used the weather as a pretext for the rise. In truth his only intent was profit. The court set him free without a fine, but warned him once. His shop lost a few customers after that. He never raised the price again for that reason.","zh":"老板想为面包的高价作辩解。他辩称面粉贵了，可没有任何凭据能证实这说法。一位公正的法官让他把数字改过来。人们要的是正当的理由，不是无力的借口。他拿天气当涨价的托词。其实他唯一的意图就是多赚。法庭放他回去，没罚款，只告诫了他一次。打那以后，他再没为这个理由涨过价。"},"label":{"tw":[["judge",0],["address",3],["attach",2],["band",6],["mark",0],["call",3],["designate",2],["pop",6],["tag",0]],"en":"In the small shop every jar had to carry a clear label. The owner would attach it with a thin band and a small tag. She had to mark each one with a price and an address for returns. People would call her the best jam maker in town, but she never let it pop her head. She would designate one shelf for the new stock. No judge could say the label was wrong. Each mark had to match the jar inside. A clean label, she said, was a promise to the buyer. It was a simple habit of care.","zh":"在这家小店里，每个罐子都得带一张清楚的标签。老板娘会用一根细带和一个小吊牌把它系上。她得在每张上标出价钱和退货地址。人们会称她是镇上最好的果酱手，可她从不让这话冲昏头。她会指定一个架子放新货。没有哪个裁判能说标签错了。每个标记都得和罐子里的东西对得上。这是一种朴素的用心。"},"link":{"tw":[["join",3],["ground",3],["shape",2],["access",6],["relate",0],["remember",3],["think",2],["direct",6],["tie",3]],"en":"The old bridge was the only link between the two villages. It would join the bank on each side and give people direct access to the market. Its shape had changed little in a hundred years, though the ground below had moved. I still remember the way it looked at night. When we think of home, the same picture comes to mind. The road and the river relate to each other through that stone tie. No screen can replace a real link like this. It holds the two banks together like a hand.","zh":"那座老桥是两个村子之间唯一的联系。它两岸相连，让人们能直接去集市。百年来它的形状几乎没变，尽管下面的地面动过。我还记得它夜里的样子。一想到家，同一个画面就浮上心头。那条路和那条河，就靠这一道石头的纽带彼此关联。再好的屏幕也代替不了这样真实的连结。它像一只手，把两岸拢在一起。"},"merge":{"tw":[["combine",0],["melt",3],["change",2],["divest",6],["mix",0],["absorb",3],["integrate",2],["venture",6],["unite",0]],"en":"Last spring two small firms decided to merge into one. They would combine their tools and unite the two teams under a single roof. The big company hoped to absorb the smaller one and integrate its workers. Over time the old ways began to melt away. No one had to divest a single shop. They would mix the best ideas from both sides. One name went on the new sign above the door. The change was not easy, and a few people left. In the end the new venture grew faster than either firm alone.","zh":"去年春天，两家小公司决定合并成一家。他们要把工具合到一处，把两支队伍并到一个屋顶下。大公司想吞下小的那家，把它的工人整合进来。日子一长，旧的做法开始融化消失。谁都不用卖掉一间铺子。他们会把两边的长处掺在一起。这变化并不容易，有几个人离开了。到最后，这个新摊子比两家单干时都长得快。"},"motion":{"tw":[["move",4],["kick",3],["change",2],["panel",6],["question",0],["reach",3],["state",2],["effect",6],["gesture",0]],"en":"At the town meeting a member rose to make a motion about the new park. She would move that the council take up the question at once. A small panel had to state its view before the vote. The first gesture came from an old man who could hardly reach the table. He gave a firm kick to the floor with his stick. The effect of his quiet words on the room was strong. In the end the motion passed, and one small change was made. The park would open in summer.","zh":"镇上的会上，一位成员起身，就新公园提了一项动议。她提议议会立刻把这个问题拿到桌上来。一个小委员会得在表决前表明立场。头一个动作来自一位几乎够不着桌子的老人。他用拐杖在地上笃笃敲了一下。他这番话的效力很强。最后动议通过，做出了一处小小的改动。公园夏天就要开放了。"},"outline":{"tw":[["abstract",0],["brief",3],["draw",2],["blueprint",6],["draft",0],["contour",3],["plan",2],["document",6],["scheme",0]],"en":"Before the builders arrived, my uncle had to draw a simple outline of the new shed. He would keep it brief, no longer than a single page. The abstract shape was enough to show the whole plan to the men. He added a rough contour of the ground and a small scheme for the roof. A proper blueprint would come later. First he checked the draft with the whole document. Two neighbours looked at the outline and asked one question. Then the real work could begin at last on a bright morning.","zh":"动工之前，叔叔得为新棚子画一张简单的轮廓图。他把它写得简短，不超过一页。那点抽象的图形就够说明方案了。他又添了一条大地的粗略轮廓和一个屋顶的小布局。正规的蓝图以后再出。他先把草稿和整份文件核对了一遍。两位邻居看了轮廓图，问了一个问题。然后就能开工了。"},"overlook":{"tw":[["drop",0],["forget",3],["lie",2],["attest",6],["miss",2],["jump",3],["survey",2],["fathom",6],["command",0]],"en":"It is easy to overlook a small mistake when a job is long. A worker may drop a number and forget to check it twice. One wrong line can lie hidden for weeks. The manager asked us not to miss any step in the survey. He would jump on the first sign of trouble. A final report would later attest that the work was done well. From the top floor you could command a view of the whole site. It took me months to fathom the size of the task.","zh":"活一长，就容易漏看一个小错。工人可能漏掉一个数字，又忘了复查一遍。一行错字可能藏上好几个星期。经理要我们别在勘察里漏掉任何一步。一有麻烦的苗头，他就会立刻扑上去。最终的汇报会证明这活干得好。从顶楼你能俯瞰整个工地。我花了几个月才弄明白这任务有多大。"},"overwhelm":{"tw":[["overcome",0],["kill",3],["beat",2],["distract",6],["drown",0],["devastate",3],["charge",2],["confuse",6],["overtake",0]],"en":"The flood seemed ready to overwhelm the whole little town in one night. Water could drown the lowest fields and devastate the small shops. Fear of the water would distract people from the whole plan. A loud charge of brown water can overtake the old bridge in minutes. We had to overcome the wish to run and beat the rising river with heavy sandbags. Noise and dark could confuse even the bravest of the men. One wrong step near the bank might kill a man. By morning the water began to fall, and we knew we had won.","zh":"洪水看样子能在一夜之间把小城淹没。大水会淹了最矮的田，也会毁掉那些店铺。恐惧会让人分心，忘了安排。一股猛水几分钟就能越过那座老桥。我们得压住想逃的念头，用沙袋跟河水拼。喧嚣和黑暗能叫最勇敢的人也乱了阵脚。错一步就可能送命。到早上，水开始退了，我们知道挺过来了。"},"pad":{"tw":[["embroider",0],["rat",3],["fill",2],["sling",6],["bolster",0],["panel",3],["paper",2],["gear",6],["tramp",0]],"en":"My sister packed a soft pad for the long train journey. She would fill it with wool and cover it with a thin paper sheet. Her plan was to embroider a small flower on the top. On the road a tramp in old gear stopped to look. A rat ran past the wooden panel of the carriage wall. She used the pad to bolster her back for the night. A sling held her heavy bag above the seat. It was a small comfort, but it made the long trip easy.","zh":"妹妹为这趟长途火车备了个软垫。她往里塞了羊毛，外面包了一层薄纸。她打算在顶上绣一朵小花。路上一个穿旧家当的流浪汉停下来看。一只老鼠从车厢壁的镶板边窜过。夜里她用这垫子托住后背。一根吊带把她的重包挂在座位上方。这点小舒服，让这趟路好走了。"},"palm":{"tw":[["handle",0],["field",3],["touch",2],["forest",6],["medal",0],["fumble",3],["tree",2],["dry",6],["ribbon",0]],"en":"She held the silver medal in her open palm and looked at it for a long time. Her fingers would touch the smooth ribbon again and again. Years before, she had learned to handle a bow in the forest near her home. At first she would fumble every shot in the wide field. A tall tree by the fence was her only mark. The dry air of summer made the work hard. In the end she won the prize. She kept the medal where her palm could always find it.","zh":"她把银牌摊在掌心，看了很久。她的手指一遍遍摩挲光滑的绶带。多年前，她在家附近的林子里学会了使弓。起初她在宽阔的场地上每次射箭都手忙脚乱。围栏边一棵高树是她唯一的标记。夏天干燥的空气让这份活更难。最后她拿了奖。她把奖牌收在掌心随时能找到的地方。"},"parallel":{"tw":[["twin",0],["echo",3],["change",2],["oblique",1],["path",6],["duplicate",0],["figure",2],["main",6],["analogue",0]],"en":"In the drawing the two roads run parallel for almost a mile. Their path looks like a twin line, one a duplicate of the other. An oblique track cuts across them near the bridge. The main figure shows how the lines never meet. A small echo of the same shape appears in the garden plan. The builder had to change one edge so the two would stay even and clear. Each line is an analogue of the other in the graph. It was a simple design, but a careful one.","zh":"图里那两条路几乎平行地延伸了一英里。它们的路径像一对孪生的线，一条是另一条的复本。靠近桥的地方，一条斜线横切过来。主要的图形显示这两条线永不相交。花园的图纸里也出现了同一种形状的一点回声。造的人得改一处边，好让两条线保持齐平。在图上，每条线都是另一条的对应物。这设计简单，却很用心。"},"peak":{"tw":[["bill",0],["head",3],["reach",2],["below",6],["flower",0],["maximum",3],["limit",2],["height",6],["top",0]],"en":"By noon we had reached the peak of the small mountain. The top was clear, and a single flower grew near the stones. From that height the river lay far below us. The climb had pushed us to our maximum, though the path was short. We had to reach the limit of our breath before we sat. My uncle held the map and shook his head at the view. He would not pay the guide bill until we were down. It was a hard day, but a fine one for us.","zh":"到中午，我们已经登上了那座小山的高峰。山顶清清楚楚，石头边开着一朵花。从那个高度看，河远远地躺在下面。这一爬把我们逼到了极限，尽管路并不长。我们得一直爬到再也喘不上气，才坐下来。叔叔拿着地图，对着这片景色摇了摇头。没下山之前，他是不肯付向导那笔账的。这一天很累，却很好。"},"phrase":{"tw":[["word",0],["ask",3],["arrange",2],["adjective",6],["articulate",0],["frame",3],["express",2],["literal",6],["idiom",0]],"en":"Our teacher asked us to explain one strange phrase from the old poem. She would arrange the words on the board in a new order. A single word can change the whole meaning of a line. We had to find the right adjective and then express the idea in simple speech. An idiom is not literal, she said, and it can confuse a young reader. She tried to articulate each sound slowly. Only then did we frame the true sense of the phrase. It was a good lesson about language.","zh":"老师叫我们解释古诗里一个古怪的短语。她会把那些词在黑板上重新排个次序。一个词就能改变整行的意思。我们得找出合适的形容词，再用简单的话把意思表达出来。她说，成语不能照字面解，会把年轻读者弄迷糊。她试着把每个音都清晰地发出来。只有这样，我们才理清了这短语真正的意思。这是一堂关于语言的好课。"},"pilot":{"tw":[["fly",0],["captain",3],["model",2],["crew",6],["original",0],["jet",3],["steer",2],["flight",6],["navigate",0]],"en":"On the short flight the pilot told us the plane would fly above the clouds. The captain would steer the jet around a heavy storm. The whole crew stayed calm and kind through the rough air. Her bright smile was an original one, and it eased our fear. She had learned to navigate the sky as a young model student. Once she let me see the controls for a moment. I asked her how anyone could ever learn such careful work. She said it was all patience and many hours of practice.","zh":"这趟短途航班上，飞行员告诉我们飞机将从云上飞过。机长会驾驶喷气机绕开一场大风暴。全体机组沉着又亲切。她那明朗的笑容很独特，缓解了我们的害怕。她年轻时是学模型设计的学生，学会了在天空中领航。有一回她让我看了一眼操纵杆。我问，这种本事怎么学得会。她说，全靠耐心和长期的练习。"},"plot":{"tw":[["game",0],["bed",3],["draw",2],["secret",6],["patch",0],["garden",3],["plan",2],["suspect",6],["diagram",0]],"en":"The family had a small plot behind the house for a new garden. We would draw a simple diagram and make a plan for each bed. My mother kept a patch for herbs near the gate. No one knew her secret plan to hide a bench behind the trees. A neighbour began to suspect that we were building more than a garden. We turned it into a game and let him guess. In the end the plot gave us more food than we could eat. He came for dinner and laughed.","zh":"一家人屋后有一小块地，想弄个新菜园。我们会画一张简单的示意图，给每个苗床定个方案。母亲在门边留了一小块地方种香草。没人知道她偷偷打算在树后藏一条长凳。邻居开始怀疑我们建的可不止是个园子。我们把它变成个游戏，让他猜。最后这块地给我们的菜多到吃不完。他来吃晚饭，哈哈大笑。"},"portion":{"tw":[["lot",0],["allow",3],["condition",2],["entire",6],["luck",0],["bit",3],["gift",2],["within",6],["share",0]],"en":"When the old farm was sold, each child got a small portion of the land. My aunt would allow my uncle to keep the whole lot near the river. The condition of the old barn made the split harder. His bad luck was that the soil there was poor and dry. He took a small bit of the field and shared it with a cousin. The entire family met to sign the paper, and a quiet neighbour gave him a gift of seeds. Within one season the poor ground began to give food.","zh":"老农场卖掉时，每个孩子都分到了一小份地。婶婶答应让叔叔留下河边那一整块地。老谷仓的状况让这次分家更难办。他的运气不好，那儿的土又瘦又干。他拿了田里的一小块，和一位堂亲合着用。全家聚在一起签了字，一位安静的邻居送了他一包种子做礼物。一个季节之内，那片瘦地就开始长出吃食。"},"pose":{"tw":[["beat",0],["load",3],["move",2],["potential",6],["lay",3],["plant",3],["confuse",2],["risk",6],["position",2]],"en":"The young model had to pose for the camera for a full hour. She would move slowly and hold one hand near her face. The heavy load of light and cloth began to beat her arms. The photographer asked her to lay a small green plant beside the chair. He could not confuse her with too many quick words. Her steady position made the whole picture calm. There was a real risk that she would grow tired. Still, the pose showed her quiet potential, and the good picture was chosen.","zh":"年轻的模特得对着镜头摆上一个钟头的姿势。她会慢慢挪动，一只手停在脸旁。灯光和布料的沉重负担开始压得她手臂发酸。摄影师让她在椅子边放一株小草。他不能用太多话把她弄糊涂。她那稳稳的姿态让这张照片很静。她真的有可能累垮。可这个姿势显出了她安静的潜力，照片被选中了。"},"premise":{"tw":[["introduce",0],["condition",3],["state",2],["absurd",6],["precede",0],["preamble",3],["presuppose",2],["context",6],["preface",0]],"en":"The whole plan rested on a simple premise: that the river would not rise. Our teacher would introduce the idea to the whole class before the test. She had to state the main condition clearly in one line. The first question would precede the long preamble of the report. A weak preface could presuppose the whole answer, which was absurd. We had to read the context before we judged the claim. Only then could we see where the argument failed. It was a quiet lesson in careful thinking for us all.","zh":"整个方案都立在一个简单的前提上：河水不会涨。老师会在测验前把这个思路介绍给全班。她得用一句话把条件说清楚。第一个问题会排在报告那长长的一段引文之前。一段软弱的前言可能预先假定了答案，那就荒唐了。我们得先读懂上下文，再评判那个说法。只有这样，才能看出论证在哪里出了问题。这是一堂关于细心思考的课。"},"preserve":{"tw":[["continue",0],["record",3],["cook",2],["establish",6],["save",0],["cure",3],["protect",2],["restore",6],["maintain",0]],"en":"Every autumn my grandmother would preserve the last fruit of the garden. She liked to cook a sweet jam and record each recipe in a small book. We had to save every clean jar for her. She would continue the old way of her own mother and maintain it year after year. A little sugar could help cure the fruit and protect it through winter. In spring she would restore the empty shelves. People came from the village to establish a new market of her goods. Her method would outlive her.","zh":"每年秋天，奶奶都会把园子里最后一批果子保存起来。她爱熬一罐甜果酱，把每份配方记在一个小本子上。我们得替她存好每个干净的罐子。她会沿用自己母亲的老法子，一年一年地把它维持下去。一点糖能帮果子防腐，护着它过冬。到了春天，她再把空架子重新填满。村里的人来买她的东西，慢慢做成了一个新集市。她的法子会活得比她久。"},"prize":{"tw":[["choice",0],["cup",3],["open",2],["medal",6],["appreciate",0],["admire",3],["see",2],["laureate",6],["prime",0]],"en":"The young writer won the first prize for her long story about a river. It was her own choice to enter the open contest. The cup on the table was small, but the medal meant more. People came to admire her work and to appreciate the quiet, steady feeling in it. She was called a young laureate by the local paper. In her prime years she would write three more fine books, she said. I could see the joy on her face. Her family watched from the back and clapped.","zh":"那位年轻作者凭一篇关于河流的长故事得了头奖。参加这个公开的比赛，是她自己的选择。桌上那只杯子不大，可那枚奖牌更重。人们来欣赏她的作品，也喜欢里面那份安静的情绪。本地报纸称她为年轻的桂冠作者。她说，在最好的年华里，她还要再写三本书。我能看见她脸上的喜悦。她家人在后面看着，鼓起了掌。"},"proportion":{"tw":[["balance",2],["rate",3],["adjust",2],["disproportion",1],["fraction",6],["dimension",0],["scale",3],["decrease",6],["ratio",0]],"en":"A large proportion of the whole family budget went straight to rent. It was hard to balance the rest with so very small a fraction left over. The rate of spending had to adjust every single month. On a small scale the trouble looked small, but it was very real. The room's chief dimension was really its high monthly cost. There was a clear disproportion between the pay and the price. We had to decrease our few small treats for a while. The ratio of work to rest felt quite wrong that year.","zh":"家里的开销里，很大一部分都花在房租上。剩下的钱要平衡，留给别的就那么一小撮，真难。每个月的花钱速度都得调整。放在小处看，麻烦显得小，却是真的。那间屋子最大的特点是它高昂的价钱。收入和物价之间明显不相称。有一阵子我们只好少买些小零食。干活和休息的比例，让人觉得不对头。"},"prospect":{"tw":[["chance",0],["promise",3],["research",2],["despite",6],["view",0],["coast",3],["search",2],["surprise",6],["scene",0]],"en":"The prospect of a quiet week by the cold coast made her smile. There was a fair chance she could really rest at last. The long view of the sea was the best scene on the trip. Despite the heavy rain, she set out to search for a small hotel. Her research on the whole area had taken a full month. She would promise herself one full day of sleep. A surprise guest joined her on the last night. It was a good, deep rest, and she came home calm.","zh":"在海边过一个安静星期，这个前景让她笑了。她总算有相当的机会歇一歇。那长长的海景是这趟旅行里最好的一幕。尽管下着雨，她还是出发去找一家小旅馆。她对这个地方的研究做了一个月。她会向自己许诺整整睡上一天。最后一个晚上，来了一位意外的客人。她休息得很好，回家时很平静。"},"provoke":{"tw":[["fire",0],["excite",3],["cause",2],["incite",6],["raise",0],["hurt",3],["annoy",2],["inflame",6],["stimulate",0]],"en":"A single rude word can provoke a whole crowd. It may excite anger and even incite a fight. The mayor did not want to raise the tax in a way that would annoy poor families. One small mistake could cause an ugly scene and hurt the town. A calm voice is far better than a hot one that can inflame the mood. Good leaders try to stimulate talk, not fear. The fire of anger soon dies when no one feeds it. Most ordinary people only want to live in peace.","zh":"一句粗话就能激起一整群人。它可能点燃怒火，甚至煽动一场斗殴。镇长不想用一种会惹恼穷人的方式去加税。一个小失误就可能闹出难堪的场面，伤了这座镇子。冷静的声音总比那能让情绪烧起来的热话好。好的领头人努力的是促成交谈，而不是恐惧。怒火没人添柴，自会熄灭。多数人只想安安稳稳地过日子。"},"puzzle":{"tw":[["beat",0],["stump",3],["game",2],["jigsaw",6],["stick",0],["riddle",3],["problem",2],["premise",6],["amaze",0]],"en":"The missing front-door key became a puzzle for the whole family. My father could not beat the clock and find it before dark fell. A simple riddle would stump even my clever sister. We turned the search into a game with a small prize. The answer was a jigsaw of clues that did not stick together at first. Her first main premise was wrong, so the problem grew and grew. In the end the key was in the flower pot, which would amaze us all. We laughed about it for days.","zh":"那把不见了的院门钥匙成了全家的一个难题。父亲怎么也赶不上在天黑前找到它。一个简单的谜语能把连我那聪明的妹妹都难住。我们把这场寻找变成了一场带小奖的游戏。答案是一堆线索的拼图，一开始怎么也拼不到一块儿。她起头的前提就错了，问题于是越滚越大。最后钥匙在花盆里，让我们都吃了一惊。这事我们乐了好几天。"},"institution":{"tw":[["institute",4],["asylum",0],["charity",3],["hospital",2],["faculty",6],["custom",2],["establish",6]],"en":"The old institution by the river has cared for the sick for more than a hundred years. It began as a small hospital run by a charity, and later a famous institute joined it. Its faculty of medicine still teaches young doctors to sit beside each patient. The custom there is to greet every newcomer with a warm drink. Long ago it also served as an asylum for those with no home. To establish such a place took years of quiet work. Today the buildings are old but full of light.","zh":"河边那家老机构已经照顾病人一百多年了。它起初是由一家慈善机构办的小医院，后来一家有名的研究所也并了进来。它的医学院至今还教年轻医生坐在病人身边听他们说。那里的老规矩是，给每个新来的人递上一杯热饮。很久以前，它还收留过无家可归的人。要建起这样一个地方，需要多年默默的努力。如今这些房子旧了，却满是光。"},"minimum":{"tw":[["minimise",4],["minimal",0],["skeleton",3],["limit",2],["maximum",1],["salary",6],["wage",6]],"en":"At the factory the manager said they must keep the wage at the minimum allowed by law. A young worker asked whether her salary could rise, but the answer was no for now. The firm hoped to minimise waste and keep the staff to a minimal, skeleton crew. There was a limit to how much they could save. The maximum output had to rise with the same number of hands. My uncle said it was hard to live on such a small sum. The owner only spoke of the market, and the room went quiet.","zh":"厂里经理说，工资只能压在法律规定的最低线。一个年轻工人问她的薪水能不能涨，眼下得到的答复是不行。公司想尽量少浪费，把人手减到最精简的几个人。能省下的钱总有个限度。同样的手，产量上限却还得往上提。我叔叔说，靠这么点钱很难过日子。老板只谈市场，屋子里一下静了下来。"},"offence":{"tw":[["offend",4],["crime",0],["attack",3],["defence",1],["adultery",6],["insult",3],["trespass",6]],"en":"In a small court the judge explained that not every wrong act is a crime. Parking on the grass is an offence, but it is not an attack on anyone. To insult a neighbour in public may also offend the law, though it is a light matter. The lawyer spoke of defence and of trespass on another person's land. He said the old rules once treated adultery as a serious offence. People in the room looked at their hands. The judge said the law changes, and so do we. Then he closed the book.","zh":"在小法庭上，法官解释说，不是每个错事都算犯罪。把车停在草地上是一种违法，但算不上对谁的攻击。当众辱骂邻居也可能触犯法律，虽说只是件小事。律师讲到了辩护，也讲到了擅自进入他人土地。他说，旧时的规矩曾把通奸当作一项重罪。屋里的人都低头看自己的手。法官说，法律在变，我们也是。然后他合上了卷宗。"},"opponent":{"tw":[["oppose",4],["opposite",0],["enemy",3],["upset",6],["adversary",0],["defeat",6],["antagonist",0]],"en":"In the school debate my sister had to face a strong opponent. They sat on opposite sides of a long table, and each had to oppose the other's plan. Her first idea upset the other team, and for a moment they lost their words. A good adversary, the teacher said, makes you think harder. In the end my sister did not defeat her rival, but she came close. She told me that a rival is not an enemy. The two shook hands and even laughed. Next year, she said, she would be the antagonist and enjoy it.","zh":"校辩论赛上，我妹妹要面对一个很强的对手。两人坐在长桌的两边，各自都得反驳对方的方案。她的第一个想法让对方一度乱了阵脚。老师说，一个好的对手能逼你想得更深。最后妹妹没能赢下对手，但已经很接近了。她跟我说，对手并不是敌人。两人握了手，还笑了起来。她说，明年她要当反方，而且会很享受。"},"inflate":{"tw":[["expand",2],["change",2],["deflate",1],["maximise",6],["balloon",0],["increase",2],["depress",6],["amplify",0]],"en":"Before the long trip, my father had to inflate the tyres of our old bikes. The pump would expand each tube and slowly fill it with air. He said we must not maximise the pressure, or the rubber would change shape and pop. It was easy to deflate a tyre by mistake with one wrong turn. A strong wind could balloon our coats and make the ride harder. He would depress the little handle and listen for a leak. An increase of ten minutes on the road would amplify every small problem. We set off at noon.","zh":"长途出发前，我爸得给几辆旧自行车打气。打气筒会把每条内胎撑开，慢慢灌满空气。他说不能把气压打到顶，不然橡胶会变形，还会爆掉。一不留神转错一下，气就漏光了。大风把我们的外套吹得鼓鼓的，骑起来更费劲。他会压下那个小把手，听有没有漏气的地方。路上多耽搁十分钟，每个小毛病都会被放大。我们中午就出发了。"},"jet":{"tw":[["green",0],["spray",3],["fly",2],["plane",6],["fountain",0],["run",2],["helicopter",6],["gush",0]],"en":"In the garden a thin jet of water rose from the old fountain. My mother would spray the green leaves with it every hot morning. Beyond the wall, a small plane would fly over the field, and once a helicopter came so low that the birds would run for cover. She said the water could gush out fast if someone turned the tap too hard. A jet of air from the pump kept the pond clean. The garden smelled of wet stone and warm cut grass. We watched it all afternoon.","zh":"花园里，一道细细的水柱从老喷泉里冒出来。天热的每个早晨，我妈都用它给绿叶喷水。墙那边，一架小飞机常常飞过田野，还有一回直升机压得很低，鸟都四散躲起来。她说，要是有人把水龙头拧得太猛，水会一下子喷涌出来。水泵送来的一股气流让池塘保持干净。园子里满是湿石头和暖草的气味。我们看了整整一下午。"},"lecture":{"tw":[["talk",3],["preach",3],["address",2],["essay",6],["jaw",0],["sermon",3],["knock",2],["speech",0]],"en":"Last winter a doctor came to give a lecture at our school. Her talk was long, but not one word of it was a sermon. She had to address a hall of three hundred students without a screen or a slide. Her jaw moved fast, and yet every sentence was clear. At the end she asked us to write a short essay about what we had heard. Someone began to preach about the old rules, and she only smiled. A loud knock on the door stopped the questions. Her closing speech was two lines long.","zh":"去年冬天，一位医生来我们学校作了一场讲座。她讲得挺长，可没有一句是布道。她得对着三百来个学生讲话，没有屏幕，也没有幻灯片。她下巴动得飞快，可每句话都清清楚楚。讲完她让我们写一篇短文，说说听到了什么。有人开始就旧规矩说教起来，她只是笑笑。门口一声很响的敲门声打断了提问。她最后那几句结束语只有两行长。"},"liquid":{"tw":[["smooth",0],["water",3],["consonant",2],["solid",1],["flammable",6],["fluid",5],["medium",3],["fluent",0]],"en":"In the lab we learned that a liquid is neither a solid nor a gas. The teacher poured water into a smooth glass and watched how it moved. She said a fluid will take the shape of anything it fills, and a good medium for heat is often a simple liquid. Some of the bottles held a flammable stuff that had to stay far from fire. She wrote one consonant on the board and asked us to keep our speech fluent while we read the list. The clear surface stayed still for a long time. Then the bell rang.","zh":"在实验室里，我们学到液体既不是固体，也不是气体。老师把水倒进一只光滑的玻璃杯，看它怎么流动。她说，流体装进什么形状的容器就会变成什么形状，而热的一种好介质往往就是普通的液体。有些瓶子里装的是易燃的东西，必须离火远些。她在黑板上写了一个辅音字母，让我们读那串清单时把话说得流利。清亮的水面静了很久。然后铃响了。"},"manifest":{"tw":[["apparent",0],["reflect",3],["appear",2],["divine",6],["evidence",0],["record",2],["disregard",6],["plain",0]],"en":"The trouble in the old factory was manifest long before anyone spoke of it. The evidence was there in every record, plain for all to see. Rust would appear on the pipes each spring, and no one would reflect on why. The managers chose to disregard the small signs year after year. It became apparent that a divine hand was not going to save the roof. A manifest of the last shipment showed how little had been sent. Then the walls began to crack. By winter, half the building stood empty.","zh":"老工厂的毛病，早在有人开口之前就已经明摆着了。证据就在每一份记录里，谁都看得见。每年春天管子上都会生锈，却没人去想想为什么。年复一年，管理者们选择不去理会这些小的征兆。后来大家才明白，不会有什么神来救那面屋顶。最后一批货的清单显示，运出去的少得可怜。接着墙开始裂了。到了冬天，半栋楼都空着。"},"manufacture":{"tw":[["industry",0],["spin",3],["produce",2],["factory",6],["construct",0],["formation",3],["chemical",6],["fabricate",0]],"en":"For fifty years the old factory worked in the cloth industry and had to manufacture wool by the ton. The workers would spin the raw thread and produce a soft cloth for the winter. A long machine would construct each roll in a slow, steady line. A special chemical was used to keep the colour bright. The formation of the cloth began with one simple thread. Some sellers would fabricate stories about the brand. Still, the town was proud of what it made. When the machines stopped, the whole valley felt it.","zh":"五十年来，这家老厂一直做纺织，得按吨生产羊毛布。工人们把生线纺出来，织成冬天穿的软布。一架长机器不紧不慢地把每一匹布做出来。还要用一种特别的化学品，让颜色保持鲜亮。布的成形，就是从一根简单的线开始的。有些卖家会编造关于牌子的说法。可镇上人还是为自家做出来的东西自豪。机器停下来的那天，整个山谷都感觉到了。"},"margin":{"tw":[["border",0],["lip",3],["space",2],["digit",6],["tolerance",0],["boundary",2],["gain",6],["perimeter",0]],"en":"On the old map, the field lay right on the margin of the town. A low wall marked its boundary along the border of the wood. My father would leave a wide space empty beside the gate, so the carts could turn. The lip of the ditch had to be checked by hand, digit by digit on the plan. He allowed only a small tolerance for error, because the land was narrow. Each small gain of ground meant a longer row of grain. He walked the whole perimeter before he began.","zh":"在旧地图上，那块田正好落在镇子的边缘。一道矮墙沿着树林的边界，标出了它的界限。我爸会在门边留出一块宽的空地，好让板车掉头。沟沿得用手一段段查过，在图纸上一个数一个数地对。他只允许很小的误差，因为这块地太窄了。每多争到一点地，就能多一行庄稼。动手之前，他把整圈边界都走了一遍。"},"medium":{"tw":[["average",0],["air",3],["state",2],["combine",6],["intermediate",0],["film",3],["environment",2],["mix",6]],"en":"Water is a medium that can carry heat through the air of a whole room. In cooking, the average cook will set the fire to medium and let the soup cook slowly. My aunt would combine three simple things and mix them in one pot. She said the environment of a warm kitchen does more than any tool. A thin film of oil on the top keeps the smell inside. At an intermediate step she would taste it and add salt. The state of the soup told her when to stop.","zh":"水是一种媒介，能把热透过空气传遍整间屋子。做饭的时候，一般的厨师会把火调到中档，让汤慢慢炖。姑妈会把三样简单的东西合在一起，放进一口锅里搅匀。她说，一个暖和厨房的环境，比什么工具都管用。面上薄薄的一层油能把香味留在里面。到了中间的某个火候，她会尝一口，再加点盐。汤的状态会告诉她什么时候该停。"},"motive":{"tw":[["need",0],["urge",3],["design",2],["intent",6],["motor",0],["theme",2],["deliberate",6],["motif",0]],"en":"In the story, the police could not find a clear motive for the theft. A man had a strong urge to take the old painting, but no one knew his real intent. The design on the frame held a hidden motif that pointed to one family. It was a deliberate act, yet it looked like a simple need for money. A small motor in the wall had stopped the camera that night. The whole theme of the book was that a want can become a crime. In the last page the truth came out.","zh":"故事里，警察找不到这桩盗窃案明确的动机。那个人有股强烈的冲动想拿走那幅旧画，可谁也不知道他真正的用意。画框上的花纹里藏着一个暗记，把线索指向了一户人家。这是一次蓄意的行为，可看上去又像只是缺钱。那晚墙里一台小马达让摄像头停了下来。整本书要讲的就是，一个念头也可能变成犯罪。翻到最后一页，真相才出来。"},"objective":{"tw":[["object",0],["goal",2],["subjective",1],["achieve",6],["aim",0],["lens",2],["imperative",6],["target",0]],"en":"The main objective of our photo club was to see the town in a new way. My aim was to catch the market at first light. Through a wide lens, a simple object can look like a small world. Our teacher said that a picture is never fully subjective if you check your facts first. It was imperative to achieve one clear image, not a hundred weak ones. The target was a set of twelve photos by June. In the end we met our goal and the show was a success.","zh":"我们摄影小组最主要的宗旨，是用新的眼光去看这座小镇。我的目标是在天刚亮时拍下集市。透过一支广角镜头，一件普通的物体也能像一个小小的世界。老师说，只要你先核实事实，一张照片就不会完全是主观的。关键是要拍成一张清楚的片子，而不是一堆模糊的。目标是到六月拍出十二张照片。最后我们达成了目标，展览很成功。"},"oblige":{"tw":[["hold",0],["force",3],["relate",2],["abide",6],["bind",0],["walk",3],["penalise",6],["accommodate",0]],"en":"The rules of the old hostel would oblige every guest to leave by ten. A sudden storm would force us to stay indoors all evening. We had to abide by the same house rules and hold our voices down. Everyone had to bind their own bag with a paper label. The manager would accommodate any guest who could not walk far, and he never used a fine to penalise the slow ones. He liked to relate a story about each room. In the morning, the sun came out. No one wanted to leave that quiet place.","zh":"这家老客栈的规矩，要求每位客人十点前必须离开。一场突然的暴风雨逼得我们整晚都待在屋里。我们得遵守同样的住宿规矩，说话也压低声音。每个人都要用一张纸标签把自己的包系好。有客人走不了远路，老板都会照顾，从不用罚钱来为难那些慢吞吞的人。他爱讲每个房间的故事。第二天早上，太阳出来了。谁都不想离开那个安静的地方。"},"obtain":{"tw":[["find",0],["carry",3],["change",2],["collect",6],["hold",0],["shop",3],["permit",6],["receive",0]],"en":"To obtain a permit for the small shop, my aunt had to find two letters of support. She would carry the papers to the office herself and hold her place in a long line. The rules had begun to change that spring, so she had to collect a new form. It took a week to receive an answer. When the permit finally came, she ran to tell the whole street. Her little shop could open at last. She kept the permit in a frame behind the counter, and every customer could see it.","zh":"为了给小店拿到许可证，姑妈得找两封推荐信。她自己带着材料跑到办事处，排着长队守住自己的位置。那年春天规矩开始变了，她只好再领一份新表格。等答复等了整整一个星期。许可证终于下来时，她跑去告诉了整条街。她的小店总算能开张了。她把许可证装在框里，挂在柜台后面，每个顾客都看得见。"},"outrage":{"tw":[["shock",0],["skeleton",3],["trouble",2],["outcry",6],["assault",0],["anger",2],["dismay",6]],"en":"When the news came out, a wave of outrage swept through the small town. The paper said a man had been attacked in the street, and the shock was felt everywhere. An outcry rose from the parents, and their anger was plain at the meeting. The police promised that no assault of this kind would go unpunished. A woman spoke of the trouble that follows such a night, and of the dismay it brings to a family. Someone raised the old law that did not even name a crime like that. The room fell silent. Only the skeleton of the old hall heard it all.","zh":"消息传出来的时候，一股愤怒席卷了这座小镇。报上说有人在街上被袭击，那份震惊谁都感觉得到。家长中间爆发出一片声讨，会上的怒气溢于言表。警方承诺，这类人身侵害绝不会不了了之。一位妇女讲到那样的夜晚留下的麻烦，讲到它给一个家庭带来的痛心。有人提起那条连这类罪行都未列入的旧法律。屋里静了下来。只有老礼堂的骨架听见了这一切。"},"overcome":{"tw":[["master",0],["kill",3],["arouse",2],["resolve",6],["defeat",0],["lock",3],["trouble",6],["overwhelm",0]],"en":"For a year my cousin tried to overcome her fear of speaking in front of a class. The trouble would arouse a deep worry in her, and the room seemed to lock her in place. She feared that one bad day would kill her whole plan. A good teacher can master such fear only by facing it, not by hiding. She had to resolve to speak once every week, even for a minute. At first it would nearly overwhelm her. But slowly she did defeat the fear. Now she stands up without a shake in her voice.","zh":"有一年，我表妹一直想克服在全班面前讲话的恐惧。这份困扰会在她心里勾起很深的担忧，屋子好像把她钉在原地。她怕有一天搞砸了，整个打算就全完了。真正的好老师，只能靠直面而不是躲避来驾驭这种恐惧。她下定决心每周都讲一次，哪怕只讲一分钟。起初这几乎要把她压垮。但慢慢地，她真的战胜了这份恐惧。现在她站起来，声音一点不抖。"},"pace":{"tw":[["rate",2],["beat",3],["travel",2],["slow",6],["step",2],["speed",3],["steady",6],["stride",0]],"en":"The old postman kept a steady pace on his daily round. His heart would beat faster on the hill, but he did not let the rate go up. He had to travel the same road for thirty years, one step at a time. A young runner would pass him at great speed, then stop to catch his breath. My uncle said the slow way often wins the long race. He would take a long stride at the gate and smile. He never once missed a single house. That was his own quiet record.","zh":"那位老邮差每天送信都保持着平稳的步调。上山时他的心跳会加快，可他不让频率提上去。同一条路他走了三十年，一步一步地走。有年轻跑者飞快地从他身边跑过，然后停下来喘气。我叔叔说，慢的人往往能赢下长跑。到了大门口，他会迈一大步，笑一笑。他从没漏过一户人家。这就是他自己的、不出声的纪录。"},"panel":{"tw":[["board",0],["window",3],["body",2],["commission",6],["jury",0],["coffer",3],["choose",2],["review",6]],"en":"A panel of five met in a room with one tall window to review the town plan. The board had to choose between two sites for a new hall. A small commission would keep the money in a locked coffer until the work began. The whole body of members sat in silence while a young man spoke. He said he was ready to sit on a jury if the matter ever went to court. Each wooden panel on the wall held a picture of an old mayor. By noon they had made their choice.","zh":"五个人组成的评议组在一间有扇高窗的屋子里碰头，审议镇上的规划。董事会得在新礼堂的两个选址之间做选择。一个小组委员会会把钱锁在一只钱柜里，等工程开工再动。成员们一言不发地坐着听一个年轻人讲话。他说，如果这事真闹上法庭，他愿意去做陪审员。墙上每块木镶板里都挂着一张老镇长的照片。到中午，他们已经做出了选择。"},"peer":{"tw":[["equal",0],["associate",3],["look",2],["portal",6],["match",0],["contemporary",3],["lord",2],["consult",6]],"en":"In the old story, a young woman had no peer in the whole village. She was the equal of any man at work, and no one could match her skill with a horse. A lord of the great house would consult her before every journey. She had an old associate in the town who ran a small shop, and he was her only true contemporary. Through the tall portal by the gate, she would look out at the fields each morning. People said she should have been born a lady. She only laughed and went back to work.","zh":"在那个老故事里，村里没有一个人能跟她相比。干起活来她和任何男人都不相上下，骑马的功夫谁也比不过。大宅里的老爷每次出门前都要向她请教。她在镇上有个老相识，开着一家小店，也是她唯一真正同时代的朋友。每天清晨，她都会从大门边那道高高的拱门望出去，看那片田野。人们说她本该生在富贵人家。她只是笑笑，又回去干活了。"},"principal":{"tw":[["head",0],["criminal",3],["capital",2],["associate",6],["lead",0],["chancellor",3],["partner",6],["main",0]],"en":"The principal of our school was also the head of a small company that sold school bags. Her main partner had once been a teacher, and a young associate kept the books. They needed capital to open a second shop near the market. Some said her lead came from a chancellor she had met at a meeting long ago. When a criminal tried to cheat them, she called the police at once. She said the school would always come first. That year the students got new bags for free. Every child in the town smiled that autumn.","zh":"我们学校的校长，同时也是一家卖书包的小公司的负责人。她主要的合伙人以前当过老师，管账的是一个年轻同事。他们需要一笔本钱，才能在集市附近再开一家店。有人说她的人脉，来自多年前在一次会上结识的一位大学校监。有个骗子想坑他们，她立刻报了警。她说，学校的事永远要放在最前面。那一年，学生们免费拿到了新书包。那个秋天，镇上的每个孩子都笑了。"},"radical":{"tw":[["base",0],["form",2],["secular",6],["root",4],["measure",2],["ultra",6],["stem",0]],"en":"In our language class the teacher explained the radical, the root of a word. From one small base, a whole family of words can take a new form. She said we should measure each part and find the stem under it. The idea was not at all ultra or strange; it was a simple tool. Then she moved to maths and drew a radical sign on the board. A secular school, she said, teaches both the word and the number. I wrote the rule in my book and used it all week.","zh":"语文课上，老师讲解了词根——一个词的根。从一个很小的基础出发，一整个词族都能变出新的形式。她说，我们应该把每一部分量清楚，再找出藏在下面的词干。这个想法一点也不极端，也不奇怪，只是一件简单的工具。接着她转到数学，在黑板上画了一个根号。她说，一所世俗的学校，词和数都要教。我把这条规则记在本子上，用了一整个星期。"},"rage":{"tw":[["storm",0],["wrath",3],["act",2],["despair",6],["fury",0],["anger",2],["disgust",6],["ramp",0]],"en":"When the great storm hit the coast, the sea was in a rage. The fury of the wind was a thing beyond any human wrath. My uncle watched from the window with a growing anger and despair. He had to act at once to save the boats on the beach. A wave would ramp against the wall and shake the whole house. Some neighbours turned away in disgust at the mess the water left. By morning the rage of the night was gone, and the sky was clear. The village counted its losses and began again.","zh":"大风暴扑上海岸时，大海狂怒起来。风的猛劲儿，是任何人的怒火都比不上的。我叔叔在窗边看着，心里又气又绝望。他必须马上动手，把沙滩上的船救下来。浪一下下撞向墙壁，整座屋子都在晃。有些邻居看到水退去后的一片狼藉，厌恶地扭过头去。到了早上，夜里那股狂暴已经散了，天也放晴了。村子清点完损失，又开始重建。"},"intimate":{"tw":[["suggest",0],["repository",3],["hint",2],["erotic",6],["familiar",0],["imply",2],["informal",0]],"en":"My grandmother had one intimate friend whom she had known since school. Their talks were informal, full of jokes and long silences, and each word would imply a whole history. She kept a wooden box that served as a repository of their letters, some of them almost too familiar to show anyone else. Whenever I asked about the past, she would only suggest that some stories are better left closed. A faint hint of perfume still clung to the paper. No one would call the letters erotic, yet they carried a warm, private feeling. 'Some friends,' she said, 'are a room you never leave.'","zh":"我祖母有一位从上学时就认识的亲密朋友。她们聊天很随意，满是小玩笑和长长的沉默，每一句话背后都藏着一段往事。她收着一只木箱，那是她们那些信件的存放处，其中有些私密得几乎不能拿给别人看。每当我问起过去，她只会暗示说，有些故事还是让它关着更好。纸上还残留着一丝淡淡的香水味。谁也不会说那些信有什么情色的意味，可它们带着一种温暖而私密的感觉。她说：'有些朋友，是你永远走不出去的一间屋子。'"},"isolate":{"tw":[["insulate",0],["segregate",3],["separate",2],["resist",6],["sequester",0],["seclude",3],["destabilize",6]],"en":"When the first leaf turned black, the gardener had to isolate the sick plant at once. He would separate it from the others and seclude it behind a glass wall in a corner of the yard. To insulate the young shoots from the cold, he wrapped the pots in cloth. Some of the stronger plants seemed to resist the disease, so he chose to sequester them for seed. He was careful not to destabilize the soil by moving too much earth at once. A neighbour asked why he did not simply burn everything. 'Better to segregate the weak,' he said, 'than to lose the whole garden.'","zh":"第一片叶子发黑时，园丁就得马上把病株隔离起来。他把它和别的植株分开，关在院子角落里一道玻璃墙后面。为了让幼苗不受冻，他用布把花盆裹了起来。有些长得壮的植株似乎能抗住这场病，于是他决定把它们单独留作种子。他很小心，一次不翻动太多土，免得把土壤弄得不稳。邻居问他为什么不干脆全烧掉。他说：'把弱的隔开，总比丢掉整个园子强。'"},"launch":{"tw":[["establish",0],["float",3],["move",2],["missile",6],["plunge",0],["open",2],["rocket",6]],"en":"The old shipyard planned to launch a new boat in the spring. Workers would move the hull on rails and let it float for the first time in the cold river. To establish the yard's name again, the owner also hoped to open a small school for young builders. On the day itself a rocket of smoke went up, and the crowd cheered as the boat began to plunge into the water. A boy asked whether it could be used like a missile. 'No,' laughed the owner, 'she only carries fish.' The launch took less than a minute, but the town talked about it for a week.","zh":"那家老船厂打算在春天让一条新船下水。工人会沿着轨道把船体挪动，第一次让它漂在冰冷的河水里。为了重新立起船厂的名声，老板还想为年轻工匠开一所小学校。下水那天，一股像火箭似的烟腾起来，船开始扎进水里，人群欢呼起来。一个男孩问，它能不能像导弹那样用。'不能，'老板笑着说，'她只装鱼。'下水不到一分钟，可镇上议论了整整一个星期。"},"liberal":{"tw":[["big",0],["adult",2],["conservative",1],["party",6],["free",0],["socialist",6],["broad",0]],"en":"In our discussion club a student called herself a liberal, while her best friend said he was more conservative. They were both adults now, yet they argued with the same heat as teenagers. One evening the topic was whether a big company should keep its prices low for the poor. She took a broad, free view and said yes; he warned about the cost. A third member, the son of a socialist family, sat between them and would not join any party. 'You two agree on more than you think,' he said. The debate ended early, and they walked home together.","zh":"在我们的讨论小组里，有个学生自称是自由派，而她最好的朋友说自己更偏保守。如今两人都已成年，可争起来还像少年人一样起劲。有天晚上的话题是：一家大公司该不该为穷人把价钱压低。她持一种开阔、自由的观点，说该；他则提醒这会带来多少成本。第三位组员出身于一个社会主义者的家庭，坐在他们中间，谁的党也不肯加入。他说：'你们俩其实比你想象的更一致。'辩论早早收场，他们一起走回了家。"},"mature":{"tw":[["age",0],["change",2],["whereas",6],["grow",0],["draw",2],["less",6],["ripe",5]],"en":"At forty, my uncle decided to go back to school as a mature student. His age did not stop him, though the young faces around him made him feel slow at first. He would draw on his years at the market, whereas his classmates knew only books. With each term the change in him was clear: he spoke less and listened more. In the yard a small tree he planted as a boy had begun to grow tall and bear ripe fruit. 'Everything takes its time,' he said. Two years later he passed his last exam with a quiet smile.","zh":"四十岁那年，我叔叔决定以成年学生的身份回学校念书。年纪并没有拦住他，只是周围那些年轻面孔一开始让他觉得自己慢。他会拿自己在集市上那些年做底子，而同学们只知道书本。每过一个学期，他身上的变化都很明显：话更少了，听的更多了。院子里那棵他小时候种下的小树已经长得高高的，结出了熟透的果子。他说：'什么都需要时间。'两年后，他带着平静的微笑通过了最后一门考试。"},"mixture":{"tw":[["mix",4],["blend",3],["substance",2],["combine",6],["variety",0],["solution",3],["motley",0]],"en":"For her rooftop garden my sister needed a good mixture of soil and sand. She would mix three parts of earth with one of fine sand, then blend in a little ash. The dark substance held water well, and the seeds loved it. The trick was to combine the dry parts first and add water slowly. Her little garden grew a variety of herbs, from mint to thyme, and no two pots looked alike. She kept each plant's food in a pale solution in an old bottle. Against the grey wall the motley pots made a bright line. By summer the whole roof smelled green.","zh":"为了她的屋顶花园，我姐姐需要一份好的混合土。她会把三份泥土和一份细沙掺在一起，再拌进一点草木灰。这种深色的东西保水很好，种子也喜欢。窍门是先把干的部分混匀，再慢慢加水。她的小园子里种了好些种香草，从薄荷到百里香，没有两个盆是一样的。她把每株植物的养分装在一只旧瓶子里的淡色溶液里。衬着灰墙，那些花花绿绿的盆子排成了一条亮线。到了夏天，整片屋顶都透着一股绿意。"},"modify":{"tw":[["change",2],["freeze",3],["add",2],["apply",6],["qualify",3],["corrupt",3],["propose",6]],"en":"The team had to modify their design after the first test failed. They would change the shape of the frame, add two small supports, and apply a new coat of paint. A good engineer knows when to qualify a claim: the result may hold only in a warm room. In winter the metal could freeze and crack, so those lines were redrawn. Someone tried to corrupt the records, but the manager caught it in time. He decided to propose the safer version to the owners and let them decide. The second test passed, and nothing was rushed this time.","zh":"第一次测试失败后，团队只好修改他们的设计。他们要把框架的形状改掉，加两个小支撑，再刷一层新漆。好工程师知道什么时候该给一个说法加上限定：这个结果也许只在温暖的房间里才成立。冬天金属会冻住开裂，所以那几条线被重新画过。有人想篡改记录，经理及时抓住了。他决定把更稳妥的那一版提给业主，让他们自己定。第二次测试通过了，这回没有一处赶工。"},"mortal":{"tw":[["individual",0],["creature",3],["organism",2],["evil",6],["soul",0],["beard",3],["beast",6]],"en":"A hunter once told me that every mortal being in the forest is afraid of something. No creature is too strong to run, and no organism lives without a hidden weakness. He had watched an old individual with a grey beard sit by the fire for hours, thinking about evil and about his own soul. In the dark a small beast came to the edge of the light and waited. The hunter did not raise his gun. 'We are all mortal,' he said, 'and that is the one truth the forest teaches.' He let the animal go, and it slipped away.","zh":"有个猎人曾对我说，森林里每一个会死的生灵都怕点什么。再壮的野兽也有逃跑的时候，没有哪个活物身上不藏着弱点。他见过一个留着灰胡子的老人，在火堆边一坐就是几个小时，想着邪恶，也想着自己的灵魂。黑地里，一只小兽走到火光边缘，停下等着。猎人没有举枪。他说：'我们都会死，这是森林教会我的唯一真理。'他放那只动物走了，它一溜烟隐进了黑暗。"},"network":{"tw":[["web",0],["system",2],["cable",6],["net",0],["fabric",2],["channel",6],["mesh",0]],"en":"A small team came to bring a fast network to our mountain village. They ran a long cable up the slope and fixed it to poles with a fine mesh of wire. The old phone system had never reached the last three houses, so people carried news by hand. Now a single channel could carry a whole class of pupils in one afternoon. The net they built was cheap but strong, like the fabric of a good coat. Slowly the web of wire spread from roof to roof. On the first night the children called their grandparents and would not stop talking.","zh":"一支小队伍来给我们这个山村接通了一个快速的网络。他们沿着山坡拉了一根长长的电缆，又用一层细密的网把它固定在杆子上。原来的电话系统从来没通到最边上那三户人家，人们传消息只能靠人力。如今一个频道就能在一下午里承载整整一个班的学生。他们搭起来的这张网不贵，却很结实，像一件好外套的布料。渐渐地，这张线的网从一个屋顶铺到另一个屋顶。头一晚，孩子们给爷爷奶奶打电话，说起话来就停不下。"},"notion":{"tw":[["opinion",0],["idea",2],["sense",6],["belief",0],["concept",2],["view",6],["impression",0]],"en":"The new teacher had to correct a common notion about the old river. Many people shared the belief that it had always been dirty, and that was only an impression from the last twenty years. She showed the class a map and asked for their opinion. In her view the water had once been clear enough to drink. The idea that a river can never heal, she said, is a concept we must drop. Her words made good sense to the pupils. By the end of the lesson several of them wanted to test the water themselves.","zh":"新来的老师得纠正大家对那条老河一个常见的看法。许多人都抱着这样一种信念，觉得它一向就是脏的，其实那只是最近二十来年留下的印象。她给全班看了一张地图，问他们怎么看。在她看来，这水从前清得能喝。她说，认为一条河永远好不了，这种想法我们得丢掉。她的话让学生们觉得很在理。到下课的时候，好几个人已经想亲自去测一测这水了。"},"novel":{"tw":[["fresh",0],["romance",3],["book",2],["story",6],["new",5],["fiction",2],["tale",6]],"en":"My neighbour spent three years writing her first novel. It began as a short tale she told her children at night, then grew into a long book of two hundred pages. The story was not a romance, though it had one quiet love in it. She wanted a fresh voice, not the smooth style of other fiction on the shelf. Every week she would read the new pages aloud to herself and cut what did not work. 'A novel is just a long letter to a stranger,' she said. When it was printed, she gave the first copy to her mother.","zh":"我邻居花了三年写她的第一部小说。它起初只是她夜里讲给孩子听的一个小故事，后来长成了一本两百页的长书。这故事算不上爱情小说，不过里面有一段安静的爱。她想要的是一种新鲜的写法，而不是书架上别的小说那种圆滑的腔调。每个星期她都会把新的几页念给自己听，把不行的部分删掉。她说：'小说不过就是写给一个陌生人的长信。'书印出来以后，她把第一本给了她母亲。"},"pit":{"tw":[["hell",0],["hole",2],["mud",6],["mark",0],["remove",2],["pile",6],["stone",0]],"en":"Behind the old mill a deep pit had filled with rain over the years. Children said it went down to hell, though it was only a wide hole in the ground. At the bottom lay black mud, and a pile of stone stood on one side where the miners once worked. My father would mark the edge with a stick so no one would fall in. He had helped remove the last carts when the mine closed. In winter a thin sheet of ice covered the water. 'A pit remembers everything,' he said, 'even what we throw in.'","zh":"老磨坊后面有个深坑，这些年来积满了雨水。孩子们说它一直通到地狱，其实不过是地上一个老大不小的洞。坑底是黑泥，一侧堆着一堆石头，从前矿工就在那儿干活。我父亲会用一根棍子在边上做个记号，免得有人掉下去。矿关掉的时候，他也帮着把最后几车运了出来。冬天，水面上结了薄薄一层冰。他说：'坑什么都记得，连我们往里扔的东西也记得。'"},"potential":{"tw":[["possible",0],["prospect",3],["actual",1],["impact",6],["likely",0],["risk",6],["potency",4]],"en":"The coach saw real potential in a quiet girl on the school team. It was possible that she would run faster than anyone in years, and the prospect excited the whole club. Yet the actual result in her first race was poor, and the impact on her confidence was heavy. She was likely to quit if no one helped her. The coach decided the risk was worth taking and trained with her every morning. Slowly the potency of her long legs showed on the track. By spring she was third in the district. 'Talent is only a beginning,' he told her.","zh":"教练在校队里一个安静的女孩身上看到了真正的潜力。她有可能跑得比这些年任何人都快，这个前景让整个俱乐部都兴奋起来。可她第一场比赛的实际成绩很差，对她自信的打击也不轻。要是没人帮她，她很可能会退出。教练觉得这个风险值得冒，于是每天早上陪她一起训练。慢慢地，她那双长腿的劲道在跑道上显了出来。到春天，她在全区排到了第三。他对她说：'天分只是个开头。'"},"probe":{"tw":[["examine",0],["hear",3],["investigate",2],["leak",6],["gutter",3],["research",2],["secret",6]],"en":"A young reporter began a long probe into a leak at the town water works. She had to examine old bills, hear from dozens of neighbours, and investigate a claim that someone had sold the pipes. The first secret she found lay in a torn note in a gutter by the road. She shared her research with a senior editor, who warned her to be careful. For weeks the story grew, and the office would not say a word in public. In the end her probe forced a full repair of the system. 'We only wanted the truth,' she wrote.","zh":"一位年轻记者开始对镇自来水厂的一处漏水展开了一场漫长的调查。她得翻查旧账单，听取几十户邻居的说法，还要查清有人把管道卖掉的指控。她发现的头一个秘密，藏在路边一条水沟里一张撕破的纸条上。她把调查的结果跟一位资深编辑分享，对方提醒她要小心。几个星期里，事情越闹越大，厂里在公开场合一个字也不肯说。最后，她的探查逼得整套系统彻底修了一遍。她写道：'我们要的只是真相。'"},"prohibit":{"tw":[["forbid",0],["bar",3],["violate",6],["veto",0],["ban",3],["regulate",6],["proscribe",0]],"en":"The club decided to prohibit phones at every meeting. The new rule would forbid taking calls and bar anyone from filming without leave. A few members said it was too strict and asked the chair to veto the change. She refused, and warned that anyone who chose to violate it would lose a seat. The treasurer pointed out that the city already had a ban on recording in public halls. It was, he said, only fair to regulate the room the same way. For a month people grumbled; then they began to talk to each other again. What the rule did, in effect, was proscribe the small habit that had kept them apart.","zh":"俱乐部决定在每次聚会上禁止使用手机。新规矩会禁止接电话，也禁止任何人未经许可录像。有几位成员说这太严了，请主席否决这项改动。她不肯，并警告说谁要是违反，就得让出位子。管账的人指出，市里本来就有一道在公共大厅禁止录音的禁令。他说，照着同样的办法来管这间屋子才算公道。有一个月大家都在抱怨；后来他们又开始互相说话了。这条规矩实际上做的，就是禁掉那个一直让他们彼此疏远的小习惯。"},"prompt":{"tw":[["move",0],["cause",2],["seek",6],["quick",0],["inform",2],["anticipate",6],["immediate",0]],"en":"A single line on the form was enough of a prompt for me to start. My teacher had written a short note that would move me to sign up for the course, and it was the immediate cause of everything that followed. She did not tell me what to do; she only asked what I was waiting for. That question made me seek an answer for days. The reply had to be quick, because the office closed on Friday. I called to inform my parents, who were surprised but glad. I had not anticipated that a small prompt could change a whole year.","zh":"表格上的一行字，对我来说就足以成为一个提示，让我立刻动手。老师写了一句短短的留言，促使我报名那门课，而它正是后来一切的直接起因。她并没有告诉我该怎么做，只问我在等什么。这个问题让我找了好几天的答案。答复得赶时间，因为办公室周五就关门了。我打电话把这事告诉我父母，他们有点意外，却很高兴。我没想到，一个小的提示竟能改变整整一年。"},"prosecute":{"tw":[["engage",0],["close",3],["act",2],["defend",1],["punish",6],["pursue",0],["apprehend",6]],"en":"The town decided to prosecute the owner of a factory that had poured waste into the river. Lawyers would engage an expert to study the water and act on the report at once. The owner hired another team to defend him in court. The judge said the law must punish those who harm the common land. The case would pursue the truth for eight long months. At last the police moved to apprehend a second man, a driver who had carried the waste. The court came to a close in June with a fine. The river, slowly, began to clear.","zh":"镇上决定对一家把废料倒进河里的厂主提起诉讼。律师们将聘请一位专家来研究水质，并立刻根据报告采取行动。厂主另请了一队人为他在法庭上辩护。法官说，法律必须惩罚那些损害公共土地的人。这桩案子追查真相，前后拖了漫长的八个月。最后警方出手逮捕了第二个人，一个运送废料的司机。六月，法庭以一笔罚款了结。那条河，慢慢地，开始变清了。"}}});
